Hand shell-owned keyboard shortcuts to the shell.

Ctrl+L, Ctrl+F, Ctrl+D, Ctrl+H, Ctrl+J and Alt+F open parts of the browser
that a shell draws for itself. With the frame hidden Chromium has nowhere to
put them -- no location bar to focus, no menu button to open -- so the key
does nothing at all.

The hook sits after the accelerator has been resolved to a command, so
Chromium's accelerator table remains the one place that says which key means
what, and only who carries the command out changes. Keys a page consumed never
arrive here, which is the behaviour Chrome already has.

Escape is deliberately not intercepted: it also stops a load, and a browser
should keep doing that. The shell hears it and closes whatever it has open,
and Chromium stops the page as well.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_view.cc
@@ -5316,6 +5316,16 @@
 
